# Biome 1, level 7 — The Fork
#
# One spring, two hubs, two paths of different lengths. The target needs both, so neither can be
# ignored, and the longer arm pays more — the length multiplier stated as a layout rather than as a
# rule. The target is 280: the long arm pays 182 for three conduits and the short one 100 for a
# single conduit, so both are needed and there is nothing spare.
#
# The first version of this level put the second hub next to the spring. Touching endpoints complete
# nothing, because a route is built from conduits, so its target was unreachable and the solvability
# gate caught it.

